apnews.com,https://apnews.com,https://apnews.com/article/php-vulnerabilities-security-threat-38d37c4c18bf8355b02d85b5a73ed642,,PHP vulnerabilities: Who's exposed and how AI both helps and hurts security,"The language that’s known as the backbone of the internet is now subject to what experts are calling the one of the most notable vulnerabilities in recent memory. PHP is the backbone of many websites. It faces significant vulnerabilities, prompting warnings from agencies including the FBI. These vulnerabilities could allow attackers to control web servers without passwords, leading to potential data theft or further attacks. PHP powers about 70% of websites, including WordPress and Drupal, making the exposure vast. Some sites, including government services, have been taken offline to fix the issues. The vulnerabilities have been known since at least 2024, but solutions stalled.",Kaitlyn Huamani,2026-10-22T16:57:00Z,2026-10-23T06:50:08.984493+00:00,https://apnews.com/article/php-vulnerabilities-security-threat-38d37c4c18bf8355b02d85b5a73ed642,static
